  "content": {
    "id": "p24-q14-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "Aziz runs beside a train track at a constant speed of 5 m/s. He notices that when running towards a train it takes 4 seconds for the train to pass him. When the train is travelling in the same direction as him it takes 6 seconds. How long is the train?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$120\\text{ m}$.\n\nEquate the train lengths calculated using the two relative speeds.",
      "worked": "Let $v$ m/s be the train's speed. The relative speeds are $v+5$ m/s in opposite directions and $v-5$ m/s in the same direction. Both passing distances equal the train's length.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}4(v+5)&=6(v-5)\\\\4v+20&=6v-30\\\\50&=2v\\\\v&=25\\\\\\text{Train length}&=4(25+5)\\\\\\text{Train length}&=120\\text{ m}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 76
  },
